---
description: PostgreSQL and MikroORM persistence rules
alwaysApply: false
---
- PostgreSQL is the source of truth for financial state and idempotency.
- Use MikroORM.
- Financial changes must be atomic.
- Wallet update and its ledger entry must be committed in the same database transaction.
- Inbox, financial changes, ledger and outbox must be committed atomically.
- Never rely on application memory for consistency.
- Never implement an uncontrolled read → calculate → update balance operation.
- Database constraints must enforce required uniqueness and integrity rules.
- The solution must work correctly with multiple application instances.
- Never change migrations directly, any changes in migrations files will be done by me via CLI